Q1. What is MVC Architecture?
Why do we need it?

Interview Ready Answer

MVC (Model-View-Controller)
is an Architectural Pattern
that separates an application
into three independent components.

• Model
• View
• Controller

This separation makes the
application easier to understand,
maintain and scale.

------------------------------------------------------------

Why do we need MVC?

• Separation of Concerns.
• Better Code Organization.
• Easy Maintenance.
• Better Readability.
• Easy Testing.
• Scalability.
• Frontend and Backend teams
  can work independently.

------------------------------------------------------------

Components of MVC

1. Model

• Represents application data.
• Contains Business Logic.
• Interacts with Database.

------------------------------------------------------------

2. View

• User Interface (UI).
• Displays data to the user.
• Does not contain
  business logic.

------------------------------------------------------------

3. Controller

• Receives user requests.
• Calls the Model.
• Returns the appropriate
  View or Response.
• Acts as a bridge between
  Model and View.

------------------------------------------------------------

