Q2. Difference between MVC
and Three-Tier Architecture

Interview Ready Answer

MVC Architecture

• Architectural Pattern.
• Separates application
  by responsibilities.
• Focuses on request handling
  and UI interaction.

Components

• Model
• View
• Controller

------------------------------------------------------------

Three-Tier Architecture

• Software Architecture.
• Separates application
  into logical layers.
• Focuses on complete
  application structure.

Layers

• Presentation Layer
• Business Layer
• Data Layer

------------------------------------------------------------

Difference

MVC

↓

Who does the work?

↓

Model

View

Controller

----------------------------

Three-Tier

↓

Where does the work belong?

↓

Presentation Layer

↓

Business Layer

↓

Data Layer

------------------------------------------------------------

Relationship

MVC and Three-Tier
are not competitors.

They are commonly
used together.

Example

Presentation Layer

↓

Controller

↓

Business Layer

↓

Service

↓

Data Layer

↓

Repository

↓

Database

